  "notes": [
    "Five sections have no instructor printed on the schedule: the two herb labs, which say only to reserve times after registration, and the three benchmark exams.",
    "Many courses run for part of the term only. The range the schedule prints is shown against each section, but it is not interpreted, so two courses at the same hour in different halves of the term are still reported as clashing when they are not.",
    "Delivery mode follows the schedule's legend: everything is in person on campus except rows marked as delivered via Zoom. The doctoral courses are Zoom by their section heading rather than by a mark on each row.",
    "The doctoral courses are listed twice on the schedule, once for current MAc/DAc students and once for Completion Module students. Section 1 is the current-student offering and section 2 the Completion Module one; several differ by date rather than by time.",
    "Version 5 prints the Thursday section of AC201 without a section number, and AC202's only section as AC202-1. Both read as numbering slips: times, instructors and section counts are unchanged from version 3."
  ],

